{"name":"Purple Illusionist","hex":"#a675fe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"illusionist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who works with illusion or sleight of hand.","One who deceives by magical or mystical means."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illusionist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magic (illusion)","blocks":[{"text":"Magic is a performing art in which audiences are entertained by tricks, effects, or illusions of seemingly impossible feats, using natural means. It encompasses the subgenres of close-up magic and parlor magic, among others. It is to be distinguished from supernatural magic which are effects claimed to be created through supernatural means. It is one of the oldest performing arts in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Hieronymus_Bosch_051.jpg/330px-Hieronymus_Bosch_051.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_(illusion)","wikidata":"Q148442"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/David_Blaine_performs_magic_for_Barack_Obama_at_the_White_House%2C_2016.jpg/500px-David_Blaine_performs_magic_for_Barack_Obama_at_the_White_House%2C_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/David_Blaine_performs_magic_for_Barack_Obama_at_the_White_House%2C_2016.jpg/500px-David_Blaine_performs_magic_for_Barack_Obama_at_the_White_House%2C_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Well known illusionist David Blaine performs magic for president Barack Obama at the White House, 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADavid_Blaine_performs_magic_for_Barack_Obama_at_the_White_House%2C_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Penn_%26_Teller%27s_Walk_of_Fame_Star.jpg/500px-Penn_%26_Teller%27s_Walk_of_Fame_Star.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Penn_%26_Teller%27s_Walk_of_Fame_Star.jpg/1280px-Penn_%26_Teller%27s_Walk_of_Fame_Star.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Penn_%26_Teller%27s_Walk_of_Fame_Star.jpg/500px-Penn_%26_Teller%27s_Walk_of_Fame_Star.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Penn & Teller's Walk of Fame Star.